3207427910207709,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we will use the concept of exponential growth. The height of the bean plant increases by \\(5\\%\\) every day. This means that each day, the height of the plant is \\(1.05\\) times its height from the previous day.\n\nLet \\(h\\) be the height of the plant two weeks ago. Since there are 14 days in two weeks, and the height of the plant increases by \\(5\\%\\) each day, we can write the height of the plant today as:\n\n\\[ h \\times (1.05)^{14} = 452 \\]\n\nWe need to solve for \\(h\\). First, calculate \\((1.05)^{14}\\):\n\n\\[\n(1.05)^{14} \\approx 1.97993\n\\]\n\nNow set up the equation:\n\n\\[\nh \\times 1.97993 = 452\n\\]\n\nTo find \\(h\\), divide both sides by \\(1.97993\\):\n\n\\[\nh = \\frac{452}{1.97993} \\approx 228.5\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the height of the plant two weeks ago was approximately:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{228.5}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{228.5}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
